  "mechanismSummary": "Protonation and loss of water give a secondary carbocation next to a cyclobutane ring. A ring C–C bond shifts onto the cation, so the ring grows from four to five atoms and most of the ring strain is released. A hydride shift then turns the secondary cyclopentyl cation into a tertiary one, which bromide traps.",
